# This file documents the SynapseOS boot sequence.
# Actual unit files are copied from each component's systemd/ directory
# by build.sh into airootfs/etc/systemd/system/.
#
# Boot order:
#
#  basic.target
#     └─ synapse_kmod (modprobe via modules-load.d)
#           └─ synapd.service          ← AI daemon (must come first)
#                 └─ synguard.service  ← security monitor
#                       └─ display-manager.service
#                             └─ synui (via graphical-session.target)
#
# The AI daemon starts before the display manager so the compositor
# can connect to it immediately on first frame.
#
# DO NOT re-add var-lib-synapd-models.mount. It came from 0.1.0, when the ISO
# shipped no model and firstboot downloaded one; it mounted a 6G tmpfs over
# /var/lib/synapd/models. The ISO has shipped a real 4.3GB synapse.gguf at
# exactly that path since, so the tmpfs did nothing but HIDE it: on the live
# media synapd started with no model, `syn status` said "model ✗ not
# installed", and every AI feature was dead — while the ISO still paid the
# 4.3GB. Installed systems were unaffected only because syn-install reads
# around the mount, from /run/archiso/airootfs/var/lib/synapd/models/*.gguf,
# which is why "the installed system works but the live one doesn't".
#
# Nothing is lost by its absence: the live root is an overlay (squashfs
# lower + tmpfs upper), so that directory is already writable in RAM if
# anything ever does want to drop a model there.
